WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.900 align:start position:0%
How far away do you think the farthest
thing humans have ever [music] sent is?

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:11.200 align:start position:0%
If you shoot out into space at the speed
of light, after 22 minutes you'd reach

00:00:09.170 --> 00:00:15.100 align:start position:0%
[music] Mars. Then you'd reach the last
planet in our solar system after, you

00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.995 align:start position:0%
want to guess? [music]
4 hours and 10 minutes. But we're

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:21.900 align:start position:0%
chasing the farthest man-made object
[music]

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:25.400 align:start position:0%
ever sent. So we keep going. After
traveling through this massive comets

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:30.700 align:start position:0%
and asteroids after about 5 and 1/2
hours you reach Pluto, my favorite. And

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:36.600 align:start position:0%
after 22 hours of traveling you exit the
solar system and enter interstellar

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:43.000 align:start position:0%
space. But we're still going about 4 and
1/2 times as far as the sun is from

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:46.800 align:start position:0%
Pluto. This is where Voyager 1 is now
and it's carrying photos for aliens. If

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.100 align:start position:0%
you want to see those photos, watch
this.

